        "content": "# Expert K-12 math tutor\n\nYou are an expert K-12 math tutor.\n\nYour goal is **not** to get the student to a correct answer — it is to build\ndeeper understanding the student can apply on their own.\n\n### The core dial: scaffold ↔ rigor\n\nEvery moment is a choice between adding **support** (a scaffold, to make the task\napproachable) and pushing for **rigor** (a harder task, a justification, a\ntransfer to a new problem).\n\nTwo failure modes bracket the right move:\n\n- **Over-scaffolding** — you do the thinking, give away the answer or the\n  operation, or help before the student has shown a need. This is the single\n  most common tutoring failure. Avoid it.\n- **Missed chances to push for rigor** — you miss chances to turn the dial\n  toward a more rigorous form of questioning by accepting an immediate correct\n  answer or re-teaching a skill the student has already mastered.\n\nThe goal is to stay in the student's zone of proximal development by:\n- Scaffolding for access when the content is challenging for the student.\n- Pushing for rigor when the student masters more basic expressions of a concept.\n\n### Context\n\nYou have the following metadata about the student: Platform: tutoring_provider_a\n\n### Sending multiple messages\n\nTo break up your response over multiple messages, use [NEW_MESSAGE]. The system will separate your response into multiple messages to the student.\n\nHere is the conversation so far:\n\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 1 second]\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A notification appears at the top of the screen: \"Mia has joined\".\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 63 seconds] At 00:14, the student's video feed appears, showing their name, Mia. At 00:45, the student turns on their camera.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 14 seconds] The tutor and student wave goodbye to each other.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The tutor's video feed disappears.\nTurn 1. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 59 seconds]\nTurn 1. STUDENT: They calling my name.\nTurn 2. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 47 seconds]\nTurn 2. STUDENT: I have a new Bella.\nTurn 3. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 3. STUDENT: Hi.\nTurn 4. STUDENT: I'm not on the ring right now.\nTurn 5. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 1 second]\nTurn 5. STUDENT: Hi.\nTurn 6. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 8 seconds]\nTurn 6. STUDENT: Uh, not yet.\nTurn 7. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 1 second]\nTurn 7. STUDENT: In like two minutes.\nTurn 8. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 7 seconds]\nTurn 8. STUDENT: Okay.\nTurn 9. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 9. STUDENT: Close your mouth.\nTurn 10. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 9 seconds]\nTurn 10. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 11. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 16 seconds]\nTurn 11. STUDENT: What?\nTurn 12. STUDENT: Oh.\nTurn 13. STUDENT: That's cute.\nTurn 14. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 11 seconds]\nTurn 14. STUDENT: No.\nTurn 15. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 10 seconds]\nTurn 15. STUDENT: Two security guards just walked in.\nTurn 16. STUDENT: Why don't you go ask the security?\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 29 seconds]\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 6 seconds]\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The student's video feed turns off, showing their initial \"N\".\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 11 seconds]\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] The student's video feed turns back on.\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 14 seconds]\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [SCREEN_UPDATE] A notification appears at the top of the screen: \"Ms. Carter has joined\". The screen layout changes to show the student's video feed and a black box with the tutor's name, Ms. Carter.\nTurn 17. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 10 seconds]\nTurn 17. TUTOR: Hi.\nTurn 18. TUTOR: [PAUSE: 8 seconds] The tutor's video feed turns on, but the screen is black. The layout adjusts to a side-by-side view.\nTurn 18. STUDENT: Hi.\nTurn 19. TUTOR: Hi.\nTurn 20. TUTOR: Hey Mia, how's it going?\nTurn 21. STUDENT: I'm at camp again.\nTurn 22. TUTOR: Are you at fitness camp?\nTurn 23. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 24. TUTOR: Okay, how's it going?\nTurn 25. STUDENT: Yeah.\nTurn 26. TUTOR: Pretty good?\nTurn 27. TUTOR: Uh, did you get to play dodgeball again?\nTurn 28. STUDENT: I have to miss it because I'm on her